TITLE:Rec Dec Traditions
H1:Rec dec traditions: two per sport room <span class="draft">plan v3 · plan only</span>
SUB:The rec dec's own traditions, for when the deck is switched on (after Pillar 5's Steps 3 and 4). v1 pitched twelve; the user kept seven. v2 offered eight more; the user answered: "2 for each room total (sports) and the talks should be closer together. Also they are small attendance. Nothing like captain addresses etc." v3 applies that: every sport room gets exactly two traditions, with two options for each empty place, and Wren talks come in two sizes: frequent small chats, and a bigger chief's talk every two weeks (the user's addition, ~02:47: "Some talks are bigger though, for chiefs etc."). Written by the Pillar 5 designer for lead 16. No game code.
NAV:read=Your answer|rooms=Room by room|talks=Wren talks|week=The week|fit=Clash check|cut=What no longer fits|q=Questions

<style>
.reading{border:1px solid var(--gold);background:rgba(233,196,106,.10);border-radius:10px;padding:10px 12px;font-size:14px}
.reading b{color:#f1dca0}
.full{color:#8fe0b0}.gap{color:#f1dca0}.over{color:var(--rose)}
</style>

<section id="read">
  <h2>The lead's reading of your answer</h2>
  <p class="reading"><b>Lead's reading (correct it if it's wrong):</b> each sport room (Lightdisc court, pool, river hall, climbing wall, float room) has exactly <b>two traditions in all</b>, counting the ones the rec deck plan already had, and Wren talks come in <b>two sizes</b>: most are <b>small chats for 4 to 10 people</b> (twice a week, any crew), and every two weeks a <b>department chief</b> gives a bigger one in the auditorium's seats; neither is ever like a Captain's address or an all-hands; the auditorium's film night and talent night are not sport rooms, so the rule leaves them alone.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Still approved, unchanged:</b> the Lightdisc Cup, Dawn swim, Wall night, Paddle club, Float hour, Glow paddle.</li>
    <li><b>Approved, changed by your answers:</b> Wren talks (small ones twice a week, a chief's talk every two weeks, a new rota below).</li>
    <li><b>Two places to fill:</b> one at the pool, one in the float room. Two options each, my pick marked ★.</li>
    <li><b>One room over:</b> the river hall's kayaks have three (Paddle club, Glow paddle and the rec plan's regatta). Nothing dropped; question 2 asks.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="rooms">
  <h2>Room by room</h2>
  <p class="note"><span class="tag new">gold</span> approved by you · <span class="tag">teal</span> already in the rec deck plan (v5) · <span class="tag old">grey</span> option for an empty place (★ my pick)</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Room</th><th>Tradition 1</th><th>Tradition 2</th><th>Count</th></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Lightdisc court</b></td><td><span class="tag">Winner Stays On</span> Sundays 11:30-16:30</td><td><span class="tag new">Lightdisc Cup</span> every 4 weeks, in Winner Stays On's slot</td><td class="full">2, full</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Pool</b></td><td><span class="tag new">Dawn swim</span> Tue + Thu 06:15</td><td><span class="tag old">★ Ring dive</span> or <span class="tag old">Captain's lengths</span></td><td class="gap">1, one to pick</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>River hall (kayaks)</b></td><td><span class="tag new">Paddle club</span> Wed 18:30 · <span class="tag new">Glow paddle</span> every 4 weeks, Sat 22:30</td><td><span class="tag">River regatta</span> every 4 weeks, Sun 09:30</td><td class="over">3, one over (question 2)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Climbing wall</b></td><td><span class="tag new">Wall night</span> Tue 18:30</td><td><span class="tag">Ring the bell</span> every 4 weeks, Sun 09:30 (two weeks after each regatta)</td><td class="full">2, full</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Float room</b></td><td><span class="tag new">Float hour</span> Wed 21:30</td><td><span class="tag old">★ Triple tries</span> or <span class="tag old">Slow stretch</span></td><td class="gap">1, one to pick</td></tr>
  </table></div>

  <h3>The pool's second place</h3>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Option</th><th>When</th><th>Who</th><th>What you do</th><th>You get</th><th>First</th></tr>
    <tr><td><b>★ Ring dive</b> <span class="note">new · playful</span></td><td>Saturdays 10:00-10:45</td><td>Rina drops weighted rings onto the Wren mosaic; four divers at a time, one a lane; 4 to 8 people</td><td>Tap a lane: you dive and come up with a ring (the swimming animation, plus a dive). Everyone gets some.</td><td>leisure and hygiene; a friendship step with whoever's in the next lane</td><td>Day 6 (your first free Saturday)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Captain's lengths</b> <span class="note">from v2 · rare, quiet</span></td><td>Every 4 weeks, Saturday 07:00-07:30</td><td>Captain Marrow swims lengths; anyone may take the next lane (2 to 4 people)</td><td>Tap the next lane: a few lengths beside the Captain, then a line or two from her.</td><td>hygiene; a little friendship with the Captain</td><td>Day 27</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <p class="note">Why Ring dive: Dawn swim is the pool's quiet one, so the second should be playful, and weekly gives the pool a Saturday crowd. Captain's lengths is lovely but the Captain-centred kind of thing your answer steered away from.</p>

  <h3>The float room's second place</h3>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Option</th><th>When</th><th>Who</th><th>What you do</th><th>You get</th><th>First</th></tr>
    <tr><td><b>★ Triple tries</b> <span class="note">new · silly</span></td><td>Fridays 19:00-19:45</td><td>Pell holds up score cards (1 to 10) while people try the triple somersault at a fifth of gravity; 4 to 8 people, the lobby watches through the glass</td><td>Tap to have a go: the float animation with a tumble. Nobody lands a triple until, one day, someone does (a ship note).</td><td>leisure and social; a friendship step with Pell</td><td>Day 12 (the Veyli guests may watch through the glass)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Slow stretch</b> <span class="note">from v2 · gentle</span></td><td>Sundays 08:30-09:15</td><td>Dr. Nandakumar leads a stretch at a fifth of gravity; 3 to 6 people</td><td>Tap to join: the float animation, slower.</td><td>energy and mood for the day</td><td>Day 7</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <p class="note">Why Triple tries: Float hour is already the calm one; a lively one gives the room its other side (the rec plan's "someone always tries a triple somersault").</p>

  <h3>If you didn't mean to count the rec plan's own three</h3>
  <p>Then Winner Stays On, the regatta and Ring the bell sit outside the count, the river hall is exactly full (Paddle club, Glow paddle), and two more places open. Options ready, so you needn't wait for a v4:</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Room</th><th>★ My pick</th><th>Other option</th></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Lightdisc court</b></td><td><b>First serves</b>: Thursdays 18:30-19:15, Pell teaches 2 to 4 beginners on the easy level; first on Day 18</td><td><b>Rally club</b>: Tuesdays 20:00, pairs keep the disc going as long as they can; the longest rally goes on the foyer board</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Climbing wall</b></td><td><b>Birthday bell</b> (from v2): on any crew birthday, 18:30-18:45, the birthday person climbs and rings the bell, friends cheer</td><td><b>New route night</b>: every 4 weeks, Tomas sets a new route; the first to top it names it</td></tr>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section id="talks">
  <h2>Wren talks: small chats and chiefs' talks</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th></th><th>Small talk</th><th>Chief's talk</th></tr>
    <tr><td><b>How often</b></td><td>Mondays and Thursdays, 19:00-19:40</td><td>Every two weeks, on a Thursday, 19:00-19:45, in place of that Thursday's small talk (and Day 8, below)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Who speaks</b></td><td>Any crew member, juniors included, about something they know or love</td><td>A department chief (or senior crew like the head of Survey): their department's best story</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Where</b></td><td>A ring of eight chairs on the auditorium stage, house dark, the stars behind; extras sit on the stage edge; tea from the utility room's kettle</td><td>The auditorium's seats, house lights half up, the speaker on a stool at the front of the stage (no lectern)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>How many</b></td><td>4 to 10</td><td>20 to 40 (a gathering, exempt from the deck's cap like talent night)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>How it goes</b></td><td>Chat; anyone can ask anything</td><td>About 25 minutes, then questions; no introductions, no Commander, never the Captain</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>You</b></td><td>Listen (the short meeting panel); ask one question for a friendship step with the speaker</td><td>Listen; one question, and a chief remembers who asked</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Skips:</b> the career's big days (1, 9-11, 15-16, 22-23, 26) and the storm (4-5), as v2 did. So the first four weeks have three talks (two of them chiefs'); from Day 29 there are two a week.</li>
    <li><b>Every Monday and Thursday has a talk</b> unless it's one of those skip days. The rota lists every talk day: in Days 1-28 only 8, 18 and 25 are clear (Mondays 1, 15, 22 and Thursdays 4, 11 are skipped); from Day 29 it's every Monday and Thursday.</li>
    <li><b>Later</b> you may be asked to give a small talk yourself (question 7).</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>The rota, the first seven weeks</h3>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Day</th><th>Size</th><th>Speaker</th><th>The talk</th></tr>
    <tr><td>8 Mon</td><td><span class="tag new">chief's</span></td><td>Dr. Imra Sato, head of Survey</td><td>"What lives between the stars": the creature everyone saw swim off at dinner (it left at 18:40). A one-off big Monday, since the whole ship wants to ask</td></tr>
    <tr><td>18 Thu</td><td><span class="tag new">chief's</span></td><td>Chief Calder, Works</td><td>"The Wren's first refit" (ends 19:45, before Echo Signal at 20:30)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>25 Thu</td><td><span class="tag">small</span></td><td>Tomas (a junior, climbing)</td><td>"Reading a route": what the hold colours mean, with a hold passed round</td></tr>
    <tr><td>29 Mon</td><td><span class="tag">small</span></td><td>Yara Esposito (Stores)</td><td>"Where every crate goes": the Wednesday delivery, crate by crate</td></tr>
    <tr><td>32 Thu</td><td><span class="tag new">chief's</span></td><td>Chief Bram Holt, Watch</td><td>"The oldest log in the Watch office": the night the Wren's first crew nearly lost the lift</td></tr>
    <tr><td>36 Mon</td><td><span class="tag">small</span></td><td>Maeve Volkov (rec dec machines)</td><td>"How the float room floats": the gravity plates, and why a fifth (the evening after crew rotation day, an easy first evening for new crew)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>39 Thu</td><td><span class="tag">small</span></td><td>Zeke Torres (Works, engine)</td><td>"How a drive coil sings": why the engine room hums in three notes</td></tr>
    <tr><td>43 Mon</td><td><span class="tag">small</span></td><td>Chef Auda Brennan (Galley)</td><td>"A spice for every port": three jars to sniff</td></tr>
    <tr><td>46 Thu</td><td><span class="tag new">chief's</span></td><td>Comms Chief Lucia Ferreira</td><td>"Messages that came home late": the longest a letter has taken to reach the Wren</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <p class="note">Then small talks from Pell ("Every disc trick I know"), Rina, the bunkmates, Envoy Saruth (a Veyli story, if you know them well) and you; chiefs' talks from Dr. Nandakumar (after the Wren cough, Days 50-53) and the chiefs again with a new story after about ten weeks.</p>
</section>

<section id="week">
  <h2>The week</h2>
  <p class="note">Only the rec dec. <span class="tag new">gold</span> approved · <span class="tag">teal</span> rec deck plan · <span class="tag old">grey</span> my pick for an empty place. "4-wk" runs every four weeks.</p>
  <div class="week">
    <div class="day"><h4>Monday</h4><p><span class="tag new">Small talk 19:00</span></p><p>the Captain's all-hands 17:45 (first Monday of a season only)</p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Tuesday</h4><p><span class="tag new">Dawn swim 06:15</span> <span class="tag new">Wall night 18:30</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Wednesday</h4><p><span class="tag new">Paddle club 18:30</span> <span class="tag new">Float hour 21:30</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Thursday</h4><p><span class="tag new">Dawn swim 06:15</span> <span class="tag new">Small talk 19:00, or a chief's talk (every 2 weeks)</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Friday</h4><p><span class="tag old">★ Triple tries 19:00</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Saturday</h4><p><span class="tag old">★ Ring dive 10:00</span> <span class="tag">Film night 20:00</span> <span class="tag new">Glow paddle 22:30 (4-wk)</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Sunday</h4><p><span class="tag">Regatta or Ring the bell 09:30 (4-wk each, two weeks apart)</span> <span class="tag">Winner Stays On 11:30</span> <span class="tag new">Lightdisc Cup 11:30 (4-wk, in its place)</span> <span class="tag">Talent night 19:30 (4-wk)</span></p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="note">Every day of the week now has something on the rec dec, and no evening has more than two.</p>
</section>

<section id="fit">
  <h2>Clash check</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Rooms:</b> no two share a room at once. The river hall's three are on different days; the regatta and Ring the bell (the wall is at the river hall's stern) alternate Sundays. The auditorium has talks Mon and Thu 19:00 (small ones on the stage, chiefs' in the seats, never both at once), the all-hands Mon 17:45-18:10 (ends first), film night Sat, talent night Sun.</li>
    <li><b>Numbers:</b> each draws 2 to 10, inside the rec dec's evening cap of about 15; only the Cup, Winner Stays On, the chiefs' talks and the shows are gatherings.</li>
    <li><b>Events plan (approved v4):</b> Day 4-5 storm: no talk that week; Dawn swim on Day 4 is before the storm. Day 8: the creature leaves 18:40, Sato's talk is 19:00. Day 18: Calder's talk ends 19:45, Echo Signal is 20:30. Day 12: Triple tries during the Veyli visit (guests watch). Day 21: the distress call (11:30-16:30) pauses Winner Stays On. Day 24: Loss of Power is a morning; Paddle club and Float hour run that evening. Day 25: the inspector is daytime; Tomas's talk is the evening. Day 27: Glow paddle, nothing near it.</li>
    <li><b>Career:</b> talks skip the big days; the weekly sport ones run as usual but aren't pushed at you on those days (no Mail nudge).</li>
    <li><b>Buildable with what exists:</b> the tradition engine's weekly and four-weekly rhythms, tap-to-join, the rec dec's animations (Ring dive adds a dive, Triple tries a tumble), the meeting panel, a speaker rota table.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="cut">
  <h2>What from v2 no longer fits</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>v2 candidate</th><th>Why it doesn't fit now</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Junior night</td><td>Takes over every room at once and is a big gathering; your answer asked for small.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Birthday bell</td><td>A third at the climbing wall (unless the rec plan's three don't count, above).</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Beach stories</td><td>The pebble beach is in the river hall, already over.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Sing-along, Night-shift matinee</td><td>Auditorium, not a sport room: outside the rule, held for now (question 5).</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Kit mend night</td><td>At the kit hire desk, not a sport room: outside the rule, held for now (question 5).</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Captain's lengths, Slow stretch</td><td>Still fit: offered above as the second option for the pool and the float room.</td></tr>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section id="q">
  <h2>Questions for the user (with my recommendations)</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><b>Do the rec plan's own three count</b> (Winner Stays On, the regatta, Ring the bell)? <i>Recommended: yes, they're traditions in those rooms; then only the pool and the float room have a place to fill.</i></li>
    <li><b>The river hall has three</b> (Paddle club, Glow paddle, the regatta). <i>Recommended: keep all three; the regatta is a race you watch, on one Sunday morning in four. To make it exactly two, Glow paddle could become Paddle club's lantern night (every fourth Wednesday, lights off).</i></li>
    <li><b>The pool:</b> Ring dive or Captain's lengths? <i>Recommended: Ring dive.</i></li>
    <li><b>The float room:</b> Triple tries or Slow stretch? <i>Recommended: Triple tries.</i></li>
    <li><b>Any non-sport traditions</b> (Sing-along, Night-shift matinee, Kit mend night)? <i>Recommended: none for now; Kit mend night is the one to bring back later if the rec dec wants a Works night.</i></li>
    <li><b>Chiefs' talks every two weeks</b> (Thursdays, the auditorium's seats, 20 to 40 people), with small talks the other times? <i>Recommended: yes.</i></li>
    <li><b>Still open from v2:</b> do you play your own Cup matches (the live Lightdisc game), and can you give a small Wren talk once you're an Engine Specialist? <i>Recommended: yes to both.</i></li>
  </ol>
</section>
